  "title": "Yen Soars Amid Bank of Japan and UK Rate Hikes, Housing Market Struggles",
  "summary": "The Japanese yen has surged against the dollar, with global markets remain jittery, while UK mortgage rates are expected to rise as inflation and oil prices drive economic concerns. Australia’s housing prices are trending down, with some suburbs experiencing the biggest falls. Japan’s central bank has raised its benchmark interest rate to 1.25%, marking its highest level since 1995, while the Bank of England maintained its interest rates at 3.75% despite rising inflation and energy costs.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Japan’s central bank increased its benchmark interest rate to 1.25% from 1%, marking its highest level since 1995, to combat rising inflation linked to global energy prices.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The Bank of Japan also reported tightening monetary policy, with the Federal Reserve and the European Central Bank raising interest rates in response to inflation concerns.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Australia’s housing prices have declined in most capital cities over winter, with some suburbs experiencing the biggest falls.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
